course: dictionary
lesson: 1837
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. In a geography lesson, coca means a bush that grows in the Andes mountains of South America. Its leaves are chewed or made into tea to help with tiredness and mountain sickness.
explain: Coca leaves can also be used to make cocaine, which is illegal and very dangerous. So when you see coca, look at the words around it. Is the sentence about a plant, a drink, or a dangerous drug? The clues will show you.
explain: On a French menu you might read «des frites et un Coca». Here Coca means a cola, a fizzy drink, not a plant. The words frites and a drink on a menu give you the clue. Always swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it fits.
fact: Coca is a bush that grows in the Andes mountains of South America.
fact: Coca tea is legal and common in Bolivia and Peru.
fact: Cocaine is a harmful, illegal drug that is made from coca leaves.
fact: Early Coca-Cola contained a little coca extract, which was later removed.
fact: On a French menu, «un Coca» means a cola drink.
exercise: What is a coca plant? | A fizzy drink made in France | A cold, rocky mountain path | A large bird that lives in the rainforest | *A bush that grows in the Andes mountains
exercise: Dani reads «Local people in Bolivia drink coca tea to help with tiredness.» What is coca tea used for? | Keeping warm in the sea | Swimming faster | Learning French | *Tiredness
exercise: On a French menu you see «des frites et un Coca». What does Coca mean here? | A bush from the Andes | A kind of French bread | A harmful, illegal drug | *A fizzy cola drink
test: In a health and safety lesson, which word names a harmful, illegal drug? | coca tea | coca leaves | *cocaine | coca plant
test: In «Coca tea is legal and common in Bolivia and Peru», which country is named? | France | *Bolivia | Australia | Brazil
exam: Coca tea is legal and common in Bolivia and Peru, but what is true of cocaine? | *It is illegal and very dangerous | It is a tea drunk for tiredness | It is a fizzy drink on French menus | It is a bush that grows in the Andes
